<title>DUBAI: Saudi distributes 5.4 mln tonnes barley in 1996.</title>
<headline>Saudi distributes 5.4 mln tonnes barley in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-03-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Arabia, the world's largest barley importer, distributed some 5.4 million tonnes of the grain throughout the kingdom last year, the official Saudi Press Agency reported on Sunday.</p>
<p>&quot;The Grain Silos and Flour Mills Organisation distributed -- of what was imported at international prices, in addition to what it bought of the local production at supported prices -- around 5.4 million tonnes of barley to consumers in the kingdom at reduced prices last year,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>Analysts expect Saudi Arabia to buy around five million tonnes of barley, or 50 percent of world feed barley trade, this year. They estimate that Saudi farmers, who are paid a government support price of $267 a tonne for their barley, harvested about 450,000 tonnes last year.</p>
</text>
